<title>USA: TABLE-Substance Abuse FY97 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Substance Abuse FY97 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p>		 YEAR</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.44     loss	 $0.35</p>
<p> Net loss		  15,473     loss	10,461</p>
<p> Revs			 2,724		    1,166</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  35,328		   29,835</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Fiscal years ended March 31.</p>
<p>Results for fiscal 1997 include nonrecurring charges of $1.8 million ($0.05 a share) for financing efforts, $2,950,205 ($0.08) related to the closure of its breath alcohol product line, $714,377 ($0.02) for goodwill associated with the closure of the company's Alconet operations and $416,421 ($0.01) for litigation costs.</p>
<p>The operating loss in FY 1997, before these charges, was $9.6 million, or $0.27 per share.</p>
<p>Full name of company is Substance Abuse Technologies Inc.</p>
